UPDATE companies SET description='Two Sisters Mill & Mercantile operates in Jeffersonville, Vermont, at The Granary on Route 15. The business was founded by sisters Monica Case and Tamra Higgins, who trace their Vermont ancestry to Revolutionary War veterans Josiah Pond and a Sheldon settler. Tamra’s purchase of twin Shetland sheep over a decade ago sparked the venture into fiber, while Monica brought 34 years of healthcare administration and occupational therapy experience.

The shop functions as a retail mercantile and community hub, stocking yarn, raw fiber, and Schacht spinning and weaving equipment—both in-store and by special order. Inventory rotates through goods from more than 60 consignors, and the sisters host free weekly fiber hours and monthly spinning sessions.

Customers include hand-spinners, knitters, crocheters, felters, and fiber tourists visiting the area. Tamra’s own flock of Shetland and Shetland/Finn sheep supplies some of the raw material sold in the store.

The founders frame the business as a way to honor the alchemy of turning land and animal fiber into crafted goods, aiming to build a fair, sustainable marketplace for livestock raisers and fiber artists. This mission drives their emphasis on in-person shopping, consignment partnerships, and community events such as a planned 2027 fiber tour of Scotland.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Yarn and fiber retail", "Schacht equipment sales", "Consignment sales", "Fiber arts instruction", "Community events"], "industries": ["Textile retail", "Craft supplies", "Fiber arts education"], "materials": ["Wool", "Yarn", "Fiber", "Shetland wool", "Shetland/Finn wool"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Schacht dealer with in-stock equipment and special-order service", "60+ consignor marketplace with rotating one-of-a-kind inventory", "Free weekly drop-in fiber hours and monthly spinning sessions", "Organized international fiber travel (Scotland 2027)", "Focus on Vermont fiber heritage and sustainable artisan support"], "facts_used": ["Location: Jeffersonville, Vermont, 4968 Route 15 (The Granary) -> /", "Founders: Monica Case and Tamra Higgins (sisters) -> /about-us", "Monica background: OTR, MBA, 34 years healthcare, occupational therapy -> /about-us", "Tamra background: M.Ed., MFA, Vermont since 1986, Jeffersonville since 1987, taught >20 years, poet, founder Sundog Poetry Center -> /about-us", "Tamra''s flock: Shetland and Shetland/Finn sheep -> /about-us", "Ancestry: Josiah Pond (Battle of Bennington), Sheldon ancestor -> /about-us", "Business origin: Tamra bought twin Shetland sheep over ten years ago -> /about-us", "Mission: honor connection of land, animal, alchemy; fair sustainable marketplace -> /about-us", "Schacht dealer, carry many Schacht products in stock, order others -> /", "60+ consignors, inventory always changing -> /", "Not an online store -> /", "Hours: Saturday 10-5, Sunday-Friday 11-5 -> /", "Drop In Fiber Hour: Tuesdays 9:45-10:45, Wednesdays 5-6 -> /", "Spinning Time: First & Third Sunday 2:30-4:00 -> /", "Scotland trip April 22 - May 1, 2027 -> /", "Email:  -> /", "Phone:  -> /", "Website: http://twosistersmill.com/ -> db"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "we are not an on-line store, visiting our shop in person (or calling or emailing for latest inventory) is always the best bet! ... one-of-a-kind inventory from our 60+ consignors", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='two-sisters-mill-mercantile' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='U.S. Outdoor Lighting operates from a modern facility in Palmdale, California, where it relocated in 2002 after originating in nearby Sun Valley. The company was founded in 1984 by Joseph Straus as U.S. Pole Co., Inc., and has spent more than four decades building a domestic manufacturing operation focused on architectural outdoor luminaires and decorative poles.

The company designs and produces LED outdoor luminaires, light poles, and architectural fixtures across six distinct product lines. Sun Valley Ltg covers traditional and historic designs; U.S. Architectural Ltg addresses contemporary site and area lighting with advanced optics; Amerilume Ltg supplies budget-friendly commercial and industrial fixtures; Ameriscape Ltg provides landscape lighting; U.S. Sport Ltg serves sports fields and courts; and U.S. Pole delivers poles, arms, bases, and accessories. Manufacturing is vertically integrated and performed in the United States, with products built to meet Buy American Act and Build America, Buy America (BABA) requirements.

Customers span architectural, commercial, industrial, sports, and landscape lighting markets. The fixtures are specified for projects ranging from gas stations, retail centers, and parking garages to city parks, school athletic fields, and dedicated pickleball or tennis courts.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["LED outdoor luminaire manufacturing", "Light pole manufacturing", "Architectural fixture manufacturing", "Decorative pole manufacturing", "Photometric design and performance testing", "Vertical integration of fabrication and assembly"], "industries": ["Architectural lighting", "Commercial lighting", "Industrial lighting", "Sports lighting", "Landscape lighting", "Outdoor lighting"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Domestic manufacturing in Palmdale, CA with vertical integration", "Buy American Act and BABA compliant luminaires, poles, and bases", "Six product lines covering traditional, contemporary, budget, landscape, sports, and pole components", "40+ years of experience in architectural outdoor lighting"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1984 by Joseph Straus -> /about-us", "Originally U.S. Pole Co., Inc., now U.S. Outdoor Lighting -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Palmdale, CA since 2002 (formerly Sun Valley) -> /about-us", "Manufacturer of architectural outdoor luminaires and decorative poles -> /about-us", "Six product brands: Sun Valley Ltg, U.S. Architectural Ltg, Amerilume Ltg, Ameriscape Ltg, U.S. Sport Ltg, U.S. Pole -> /about-us", "Domestic manufacturing, vertical integration, Buy American Act/BABA compliant -> /about-us", "UL Listed certification -> db", "Serves architectural, commercial, industrial, sports, landscape markets -> /about-us", "Examples: gas stations, retail, parking garages, city parks, school fields, pickleball/tennis courts -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "leading manufacturer of architectu