UPDATE companies SET description='US LED, Ltd. is a manufacturer of commercial and industrial LED lighting fixtures and controls headquartered in Katy, Texas, a suburb of Houston. The company was founded in 2001 by Ron Farmer, who serves as CEO, and initially focused on LED sign lighting before expanding into general illumination in 2009.

The company designs, engineers, and assembles its products in-house at its Katy facility, employing between 51 and 200 people. Its portfolio includes indoor and outdoor fixtures, LED lamps, refrigeration and emergency exit lighting, sports lighting, sign cabinet and channel letter lighting, track lighting, power supplies, and lighting controls. US LED also provides lighting audits, photometric layouts, project management, turnkey installation, rebate management, and ROI analysis, and has completed more than 50,000 projects nationwide.

US LED serves a broad range of commercial and industrial sectors, including retail, hospitality, education, municipal and infrastructure, office and corporate campuses, self‑storage, sports venues, warehouses, auto dealerships, and convenience stores. Its customers range from Fortune 500 companies to regional businesses undertaking national multi‑site rollouts.

The company emphasizes ultra‑long‑life LED products rated up to 200,000 hours (L70), backed by a ten‑year warranty, and positions itself as a direct manufacturer that eliminates distribution markups. Its differentiators include on‑site engineering and 100 % testing, a nationwide network of certified installers for turnkey projects, and operational‑efficiency services such as HVAC optimization, energy management systems, and demand‑response programs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom LED fixture manufacturing", "In-house engineering and R&D", "100% product testing", "USA assembly", "Lighting audit services", "Lighting layout and photometric design", "Project management", "Turnkey installation", "Rebate management", "ROI analysis", "Lighting as a Service (LaaS)", "HVAC system optimization", "Energy management system implementation", "Demand response program management", "Active load management"], "industries": ["commercial", "industrial", "retail", "hospitality", "auto dealership", "convenience store", "education", "municipal", "infrastructure", "office", "corporate campus", "self-storage", "sports venues", "warehouses"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Assembled in the USA (Katy, Texas)", "In-house engineering and 100% product testing", "10-year warranty on products", "Nationwide turnkey installation and project management", "Direct manufacturer eliminating distribution markups"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 -> db", "Headquarters in Katy, Texas -> db", "Employee count 51-200 -> db", "Manufacturer of commercial and industrial LED lighting fixtures and controls -> db", "Assembled in-house in Katy, Texas -> /", "In-house engineering and 100% product testing -> /", "Product portfolio includes indoor/outdoor fixtures, lamps, refrigeration, emergency, sports, sign, channel letter, track, power supplies, controls -> /", "Services: lighting audits, layouts, project management, installation, rebate management, ROI analysis, Lighting as a Service -> /", "Industries served: commercial, industrial, retail, hospitality, auto dealership, convenience store, education, municipal, infrastructure, office, corporate campus, self-storage, sports venues, warehouses -> /", "Completed 50,000+ projects nationwide -> /about-us", "Ultra-long-life LED up to 200,000 hours L70 -> /", "10-year warranty -> /", "Nationwide turnkey installation network -> /", "Direct manufacturer eliminating distribution markups -> /", "Operational efficiency solutions: HVAC optimization, energy management, demand response -> /about-us", "CEO Ron Farmer mentioned -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "US LED is a Katy, Texas-headquartered manufacturer of commercial and industrial LED lighting fixtures and controls, assembled in-house since 2001", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "51-200", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/usled"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='us-led-ltd' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='US Semiconductor is headquartered in Palm Bay, Florida. The company operates as a microelectronics component supplier and upstream pathway architect, engaging early in the architecture process to help aerospace, defense, space, and safety-critical programs determine viable semiconductor strategies. No founding year or ownership details are publicly disclosed.

The firm supplies a range of microelectronics component families including memory (EEPROM, UVEPROM, SRAM, serial memory), FPGAs, processors and microcontrollers, analog and power management devices, and interfaces and mixed-signal components. Beyond component supply, US Semiconductor provides engineering services such as qualification strategy alignment, component trade studies, radiation-conscious component strategy, obsolescence and lifecycle planning, and supply chain and sourcing strategy. The company does not operate as a testing laboratory, certification authority, or system integrator.

US Semiconductor serves programs across space systems (satellite platforms, exploration missions, constellation architectures), aerospace and defense (avionics platforms, defense electronics, mission-critical control systems), and industrial and safety-critical systems (infrastructure, energy platforms, transportation control, safety monitoring). Its customers are engineering and program teams facing compressed acquisition cycles, radiation exposure constraints, and long deployment timelines.

The company differentiates itself by engaging upstream before architecture hardens, aligning semiconductor selection with mission exposure, qualification boundaries, and lifecycle continuity. This early pathway determination aims to prevent redesign, delays, and supply disruption during program deployment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Qualification Strategy & Alignment", "Component Trade Studies & Selection", "Radiation-Conscious Component Strategy", "Obsolescence & Lifecycle Planning", "Supply Chain & Sourcing Strategy", "PEM Qualification", "Hi-Rel & Radiation-Exposed Systems Support", "Program Sustainment & Lifecycle Support", "Flight-Critical Avionics Component Architecture", "GN&C & Mission Control Electronics Component Architecture", "Payload & Mission Electronics Component Architecture"], "industries": ["Space Systems", "Aerospace & Defense", "Industrial & Safety-Critical Systems", "Aerospace / Avionics", "Military / Defense Platform", "Medical Device / System", "Power / Energy System", "Ground / Defense", "Medical / Regulated", "Space / Satellite System", "Industrial / Safety-Critical System", "Communications / Networking"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Engages upstream in architecture process to define component pathways before constraints lock in", "Aligns semiconductor selection with mission exposure, qualification boundaries, and lifecycle continuity", "Provides radiation-conscious component strategy treating radiation as a design variable", "Offers obsolescence and lifecycle planning to preserve configuration stability", "Operates as component supplier and pathway architect, not a lab or prime integrator"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Palm Bay, Florida -> db", "Business description: microelectronics component supplier and upstream pathway architect -> /about-us", "Component families: memory, FPGAs, processors, analog & power, interfaces & mixed-signal -> /", "Engineering services: qualification strategy, trade studies, radiation-conscious strategy, obsolescence planning, supply chain strategy -> /capabilities", "Industries served: space systems, aerospace & defense, industrial & safety-critical -> /about-us", "Not a laboratory, certification authority, or system integrator -> /about-us", "Differentiation: upstream engagement, alignment with mission exposure and lifecycle continuity -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a component supplier and upstream pathway architect.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='us-semiconductor' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company became part of US Clean Energy, a private holding company focused on distributed power generation, in 2023.

The firm develops, owns, operates, finances, and manages subscriptions for community solar, battery energy storage systems (BESS), and distributed power projects. As of 2026, it has completed over 350 MW of distributed generation, has more than 2 GW active or in development across 14 states, serves 15,000-plus community solar subscribers, and has produced 1 billion kWh of clean energy. The team numbers 90-plus.

Its solutions serve households, businesses, municipalities, landowners, utilities, and large corporations such as Walmart. Notable partnerships include serving as the official solar partner of the Minnesota Twins and supporting Colorado nonprofits like Bridge House with workforce training.

US Solar emphasizes its role as a long-term, independent owner-operator with an end-to-end model that delivers localized energy solutions. The company highlights community benefits including agrivoltaics, pollinator habitat, soil health improvements, and over $1 million committed to community impact initiatives.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Community solar development", "Community solar subscription management", "Energy storage (BESS) development and operation", "Distributed power project development", "Project financing", "Agrivoltaics integration", "Pollinator habitat creation", "Landowner lease solutions", "Utility grid solutions", "Workforce development programs"], "industries": ["Community solar", "Energy storage", "Distributed power", "Clean energy", "Agrivoltaics", "Utility services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Long-term independent owner-operator model", "End-to-end development, ownership, operation, financing, and subscription management", "Agrivoltaics and dual-use land practices (pollinator habitat, soil health)", "Over $1 million committed to community impact initiatives", "1 billion kWh of clean energy produced to date"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2014 -> /about", "Headquarters in Minneapolis, Minnesota -> db", "90+ employees -> /about", "15,000+ community solar subscribers -> /about", "350+ MW DG completed -> /", "2+ GW active & in development -> /", "14 markets nationwide -> /", "1B kWh clean energy production to date -> /", "Part of US Clean Energy since 2023 -> /about", "Leadership: Martin Mobley (CEO), Reed Richerson (President), Shawn Mobley (President & COO), Bruce Bedwell (General Counsel), Brian Lantz (CFO), Erica Forsman (CCO) -> /about", "Services: community solar, energy storage, distributed power -> /about and /", "Differentiators: long-term independent owner-operator, end-to-end model -> /about", "Community impact: agrivoltaics, pollinator habitat, $1M committed -> /", "Customers: households, businesses, municipalities, landowners, utilities, corporations -> / and /about", "Minnesota Twins partnership -> / (products list)", "Walmart mention (Mark Vanderhelm) -> db (industries_served)"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "US Solar is a national developer, owner, operator, financier, and subscription manager of community solar, energy storage, and distributed power projects working to address our country''s evolving energy needs.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "90+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/ussolarcorporation/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='us-solar-united-states-solar-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='US Titan Manufacturing operates from Fort Morgan, Colorado, as a division of Midwestern Millwright, a millwright and fabrication firm established in 1997. The company leverages nearly three decades of hands-on experience in industrial and food processing equipment.

The shop designs and builds conveyor systems, meat processing equipment such as viscera tables, head chiseler tables, hoppers, process and hydraulic tanks, and paunch pumps, along with sanitizing stations and personnel platforms. In-house capabilities span CAD design, 3D modeling, 3D laser scanning, precision fabrication, machining, and waterjet cutting held to ±0.005″ tolerance. A dedicated team of engineers, welders, and assemblers handles projects from concept through turnkey installation, including millwright services, structural steel erection, and grain handling systems.

Primary customers serve the food processing, meat packing, agricultural, oil & gas, and heavy industrial sectors. Concrete examples include custom conveyors for meat packing plants, sanitary stainless steel tables and sinks for food production lines, and overhead chain conveyors with custom sprockets for processing facilities across the Midwest and beyond.

