UPDATE companies SET description='A carpenter''s son from Red Lodge, Montana, Robichaud began sweeping shop floors at age ten and built his first log chair from driftwood at sixteen. After years working on log homes across Montana and Idaho — including a 15,000‑square‑foot residence in Big Sky and cabins at Twelve Springs Ranch — he launched a side business crafting log furniture from reclaimed materials. The recession of 2009 forced a pivot: a bed built from roadside timber sold quickly on Craigslist, and the company replaced his carpentry income within months.

Today the shop produces custom rustic furniture, cabinets, curved staircases, and architectural trim, with roughly 95 percent of output made to order. Every step — from gathering naturally seasoned logs in flash‑burn areas to final finishing — is performed in‑house, allowing control over quality and sustainability. The company also undertakes remodel and new‑construction woodworking, subcontracting only licensed trades such as plumbing and electrical.

The customer base is primarily residential, serving homeowners across Idaho and neighboring states, with shipments reaching Texas, California, Alaska, and British Columbia. Builders and designers also engage the firm for custom cabinetry and stairwork on high‑end homes in the Treasure Valley and resort communities like Tamarack and McCall.

Robichaud''s founding ethos remains central: using dead, dry logs removed from fire‑prone zones both reduces wildfire risk and yields stable, character‑rich material. The company emphasizes affordable, heirloom‑grade pieces built to last, with a small rotating inventory of pre‑made beds and furniture available for immediate purchase.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom rustic log furniture", "Cabinet making", "Curved staircase construction", "Custom trim and finish carpentry", "Log collection and preparation", "In-house finishing", "Remodel and new construction woodworking"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Custom cabinetry", "Architectural woodwork", "Log home construction"], "materials": ["Sustainably sourced logs", "Dead dry logs from flash burn areas", "Barnwood", "Driftwood", "Seasoned logs", "Scrap wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Sustainably sourced logs from flash\u2011burn areas", "95% custom work with full in\u2011house log\u2011to\u2011finish process", "Affordable heirloom\u2011grade rustic furniture and cabinetry", "Pre\u2011made items in stock for quick turnaround", "Ships throughout the U.S. and Canada"], "facts_used": ["Founded by Aaron Robichaud in Boise, Idaho in 2009 -> /about-us", "Aaron Robichaud background: carpenter''s son, first log chair at 16 -> /about-us", "Worked on log homes in Montana and Idaho, including 15,000 sq ft home and Twelve Springs Ranch -> /about-us", "Started side business building log furniture from reclaimed materials -> /about-us", "Recession 2009: built bed from roadside wood, sold on Craigslist, started Unique Western Woodworks -> /about-us", "95% custom made, in-house from log collection to finish -> /about-us", "Sustainably sourced raw materials, logs from flash burn areas -> /about-us and /", "Serves customers across Idaho, surrounding states, Texas, California, Alaska, British Columbia -> /about-us", "Also serves builders/designers for high-end homes in Treasure Valley, Tamarack, McCall -> /about-us", "Pre-made items like beds available for immediate sale -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Middleton, Idaho -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We do the work on every project from start to finish. Every step to create our furniture and cabinets are all done \u2018in house\u2019, including collecting all the logs we use, building the projects, and applying the finish for completion.", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='unique-western-woodworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
